19:04:54 said  I refined the terminal control panel so it gives you a clear, live view of your servers and app containers, with usage, cost estimates, projections, and detailed tabs for logs, cost breakdown, configuration details, and a 7-day outlook. You can move between panels, switch the detail views, add a new server, remove one with a safety confirmation that shows the financial impact, and simulate extra load to see the numbers react.
19:04:54 said  The interface is fully usable now, but the live figures come from a realistic built-in simulation because real connections to your servers and container environments aren’t wired in yet, and some broader views are still simple placeholders. Everything builds and checks cleanly with no warnings.
19:04:54 said  A good next step would be to connect it to your real servers so it can show actual containers, live measurements, and true costs from your environment.
